    <textTemplates>
        <name>TTDefaultStartPrompt</name>
        <isViewedAsPlainText>false</isViewedAsPlainText>
        <text>&lt;p&gt;Below is a list of Contact Info Relationships Opportunity Contact Roles relationships and Campaigns from responded campaign members from Salesforce NPSP contact.  Please write a summary of this person&apos;s history in the format of a donor brief I can share with our CEO/Development Officers so they can quickly prepare for a meeting. &lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </textTemplates>
    <textTemplates>
        <name>TTOpportunityDefault</name>
        <isViewedAsPlainText>false</isViewedAsPlainText>
        <text>&lt;p&gt;Our org&apos;s sales processes are defined here&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Donation sales process &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pledged = made a written commitment - most pledges are collected 95% of the time but  cash in is based on the first payment date vs the last payment date&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Closed/Won = All cash has been collected&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Declined = This means the donor originally pledged the gift but reneged on the obligation - it&apos;s unlikely this donor would give again unless the closed lost reason field indicates otherwise&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Grant Sales Process&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Prospecting  = We have not engaged with  the donor we&apos;re doing research&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;LOI Submitted = We&apos;ve submitted a letter of intent by some means formal or informal&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Application Submitted = The grant has been applied for, either the donor has given a go-ahead on the LOI or there was an open application process&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Awarded = Closed/Won &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Withdrawn = We have decided to withdraw our application  - refer to the closed lost/reason field for context on the strength of our relationship &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Declined = In this context it means the donor has said no on our application, we may have lost the grant to another nonprofit but its possible the grant was cancelled see the closed lost reason for context&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Major Gift Sales process&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;similar to donation sales process with these differences - major gifts generally take more effort to cultivate over a longer period &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Identification = We&apos;re thinking of doing research on this donor&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Qualification = we&apos;re doing research&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cultivation = &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt; same as prospecting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Solicitation = we&apos;ve made an ask&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Proposal/Review = we&apos;re negotiating the ask&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verbal Commitment = we got a commitment that is not legally binding - this is not a grant so there&apos;s no &quot;pledged&quot; stage&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Awarded = This means we&apos;ve received a written commitment or at least partial payment&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Closed Won = same as above&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Withdrawn = same as above&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Declined = same as above&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </textTemplates>
